# === Work laptop SSH (BT-LW1180) ===========================================
# Inbound to BT-LW1180 always hits sshjohn at the wire level — sshd cannot
# authenticate AAD users (~/notes/work-laptop-ssh-aad.md explains why). The
# `work*` aliases below chain through sshjohn into an inner sshd that runs
# inside BT\john.hamlin's live RDP session, bound to localhost:2222. Full
# design in ~/notes/work-laptop-ssh-jh-nested.md.

# Default: drops into MSYS2 fish as BT\john.hamlin. The everyday alias.
# The fish-launcher.cmd mirrors the WezTerm fast-launch pattern: sets just
# MSYSTEM/CHERE_INVOKING/MSYS2_PATH_TYPE/HOME/PATH and execs fish.exe directly,
# bypassing bash, msys2_shell.cmd, and /etc/profile. See ~/notes/fish-setup.md
# for the WezTerm-side rationale and ~/notes/work-laptop-ssh-jh-nested.md for
# how the env vars sshjohn used to need are no longer required here.
Host work
    HostName localhost
    Port 2222
    User john.hamlin
    ProxyJump work-sshjohn-vscode
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    RequestTTY yes
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    UserKnownHostsFile ~/.ssh/known_hosts.work-jh
    RemoteCommand "C:\Users\john.hamlin\.ssh-inner\fish-launcher.cmd"
    # No ControlMaster on inner hop — see work-ps for why.

# Same target, drops into pwsh 7 (or whatever the inner sshd's ForceCommand
# routes to when SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND is empty). Use for pwsh work, VS Code
# Remote-SSH, scp, rsync — anything that wants a clean shell without a
# RemoteCommand hijack.
Host work-ps
    HostName localhost
    Port 2222
    User john.hamlin
    ProxyJump work-sshjohn-vscode
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    RequestTTY auto
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    UserKnownHostsFile ~/.ssh/known_hosts.work-jh
    # NO ControlMaster on the inner hop — Win32-OpenSSH's channel
    # multiplexing returns stale output from previous slaves
    # (tested 2026-05-28, every reused slave returned the prior command's
    # stdout instead of its own). The outer hop's ControlMaster on
    # work-sshjohn-vscode handles connection reuse fine on its own.

# Legacy: SSH as sshjohn into the existing MSYS2-with-env-snapshot setup
# (ssh-shell.cmd on the Windows side). Was the default; kept as an escape
# hatch if the inner sshd is down. Files written here are owned by sshjohn,
# not john.hamlin — use `work` instead for any normal use.
Host work-sshjohn
    HostName 10.10.10.12
    User sshjohn
    RequestTTY yes
    RemoteCommand C:\Users\john.hamlin\local-admin\scripts\ssh-shell.cmd

# Legacy: SSH as sshjohn with a clean shell (no RemoteCommand, no forced TTY).
# Also the ProxyJump host for the `work` and `work-ps` aliases above. Only
# use directly when fixing something broken with the inner sshd; everything
# else is better served by `work` or `work-ps`.
#
# ControlMaster: keep the outer hop's TCP+SSH session warm for 10 minutes
# after the last child exits. Massively cuts latency for repeated `wkt`,
# `ssh work-ps cmd`, scp, etc — each subsequent connection reuses the
# already-authenticated outer tunnel and only pays the inner-sshd auth cost.
# Without this, each `ssh work` is two full kex + auth round trips.
# 2026-06-15: repointed from the LAN IP 10.10.10.12 to the laptop's Tailscale
# address. The LAN IPv4 path went dark (ping 100% loss, port 22 timeout) while
# the SAME machine answered fine over Tailscale + IPv6 and ARP stayed REACHABLE
# — i.e. the laptop's Windows Firewall is dropping inbound IPv4 on the LAN
# (network profile flipped to Public on a Wi-Fi reconnect). Tailscale's direct
# datapath rides the local IPv6 (~6ms), so no real latency cost. To revert to
# LAN once the firewall profile is fixed, swap HostName back to 10.10.10.12.
Host work-sshjohn-vscode
    HostName 100.114.178.68
    User sshjohn
    RequestTTY no
    RemoteCommand none
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-%r@%h:%p
    ControlPersist 10m
    # Keepalives so a master left holding a dead TCP session (e.g. after a
    # laptop reboot) self-terminates in ~90s instead of hanging forever and
    # wedging every new connection that multiplexes onto it. See the stale
    # ControlMaster writeup in ~/notes/btnet-socks-chrome.md (2026-06-23).
    ServerAliveInterval 30
    ServerAliveCountMax 3

# --- Dedicated outer hop for the long-lived tunnels (SOCKS :1080, -L 443) ---
# Identical to work-sshjohn-vscode BUT with no ControlMaster: the tunnels are
# single long-lived connections that gain nothing from multiplexing, and
# sharing the interactive master is what coupled them to its stale-socket
# wedge after a reboot. With their own un-multiplexed connection + keepalives,
# a stale *interactive* cm-sshjohn socket can never wedge the tunnels, and
# each tunnel deterministically reconnects (systemd Restart=always) once the
# laptop + RDP session are back. Used by btnet-socks-tunnel/btnet-tunnel units.
Host work-sshjohn-tunnel
    HostName 100.114.178.68
    User sshjohn
    RequestTTY no
    RemoteCommand none
    ControlMaster no
    ControlPath none
    ServerAliveInterval 30
    ServerAliveCountMax 3

Host work-tunnel
    HostName localhost
    Port 2222
    User john.hamlin
    ProxyJump work-sshjohn-tunnel
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    RequestTTY no
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    UserKnownHostsFile ~/.ssh/known_hosts.work-jh
    ControlMaster no
    ControlPath none

